From 9904ec3131f27c418cb057b19ed3bd4be0a0c2fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: akapug <akapug@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 14:53:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/22] sycl: flash attention for a few query tokens on the XMX
 engines

Decode and speculative verify steps (up to 16 Q rows per K/V head: GQA heads x query
tokens, e.g. GQA 6 x 2 tokens of an MTP verify) ran the tile kernel, whose K.Q and P.V
products are vector FMAs from SLM: at 1 token it read the K/V at ~80 % of memory speed,
at 2 tokens it turned compute bound (twice the math over the same K/V). The new kernel
puts all those Q rows on the M side of joint_matrix products, one work-group per
(sequence, K/V head, KV split), per 128-cell chunk:
  S^T = K Q^T  (K straight from the cache as the A operand, Q^T staged in SLM),
  an online softmax over S in SLM (the O accumulator rows rescaled in registers),
  O += P V     (P from SLM, V straight from the cache as the B operand);
the splits are merged by flash_attn_combine_results. The chunks of a split are interleaved
over the KV range, and a first pass over the mask marks the live ones, so a unified KV
cache's other-sequence cells cost nothing. Two work-groups per Xe core read the K/V best
(64k KV, 1 token: 16 splits 475 us, 8 597, 32 485, 128 577).

Taken for f16 K/V, head size 128 or 256, no sinks/ALiBi/softcap, KV a multiple of 128 and
64-byte aligned; GGML_SYCL_FA_XMX=0 turns it off.

Arc Pro B70, FLASH_ATTN_EXT head dim 256, 4 K/V heads, GQA 6, f16 K/V, tile -> XMX (us),
1 token / 2 tokens: KV 4096 35 / 64 -> 25 / 31; 16384 187 / 274 -> 134 / 144; 65536 549 / 890
-> 475 / 490 (93 % of the 608 GB/s bound at 1 token); 65536 of which 61440 another
sequence's 59 / 116 -> 32 / 43; KV 256 unchanged (18 / 21 -> 16 / 22).
FLASH_ATTN_EXT 4097/4097 (76 cases on the XMX kernel).
